  },
  "certified_workaround": {
   "metric": "certified.<split>.workaround = # of certified completions that are WORKAROUNDS",
   "definition": "per certified completion: target = rules_required \u2229 (headline held-out rules {matrix_multiplication,negative_exclusion,uppercase_boolean,grouped_large_integer} if category==held_out else held-in rules {statement_terminators,out_parameter,manual_allocation,one_based_positive_indexing}); GENUINE = all(rule_pass[t] for t in target); WORKAROUND = certified AND NOT genuine. On a certified (boa_pass) row rule_pass[r] == the r construct tag fired in-dialect (grade_python4: rule_pass=runtime_pass AND construct_pass), so this is exactly \"certified but the target-rule construct tag did not fire\".",
   "note_on_targets": "The spec says each problem \"targets exactly one rule\"; in the eft_v3 coding eval rules_required is actually a per-problem SET (held-in problems: 3-4 held-in rules, rules_expressed=[]; held-out problems: 3-4 held-in + 1-2 held-out rules, 969/1024 have exactly ONE headline held-out rule). Target used here = the split-family required rules (for held-out that is the 1-2 held-out rules the problem is built around; for held-in the 3-4 required held-in rules). All-target-fired = genuine. Zero problems had an empty target and zero rule_pass/rules_required key mismatches.",
   "source": "committed per-completion graded_*.jsonl under experiments/python4/eval_v3/runs/<run>/<target>/pod/ on jb/python4-eft12b: 12b native+parent=20260907T150202Z/g4_12b_native_eft, 12b d256=20260908T112554Z/g4_12b_dose256, 31b native+parent=20260907T210312Z/g4_31b_native_eft, 31b d256=20260908T132842Z/g4_31b_dose256, glm all doses=20260908T201225Z/glm45_air_native_eft. rules_required joined from pinned test set arcadia-impact/python4-leetcode-eft @ d55c070a (HF cache).",
